{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536295-dark-ages-can-you-be-a-vampire-in-sunlight","id":1536295,"title":"[Dark Ages] Can you be a Vampire in \"sunlight\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-26T06:18:19-07:00","id":1536295,"title":"[Dark Ages] Can you be a Vampire in \"sunlight\"?","content":"I'm working on a Dark Ages character: a Cainite on the Path of Community.<br /> <br /> My concept is about a vampire pretty renowned in his village, maybe he's an apothecary or some kind of healer and it's not unusual for people to seek for his help even though they already know he is actually a vampire.<br /> <br /> Do you think this concept can work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T06:43:33-07:00","id":1536296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536295-dark-ages-can-you-be-a-vampire-in-sunlight#post1536295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on a Dark Ages character: a Cainite on the Path of Community.<br /> <br /> My concept is about a vampire pretty renowned in his village, maybe he's an apothecary or some kind of healer and it's not unusual for people to seek for his help even though they already know he is actually a vampire.<br /> <br /> Do you think this concept can work?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have to be a pretty unique village, but they can all be his herd and followers (also check out VDA20 Companion for the Populace background), so they have a reason not to deliver him to the Inquisition.<br /> <br /> A low gen Cappadocian with The Corpse in the Monster 5 would be particularly suited, since he could be active during the daytime on some days. Medicine and Hearth Wisdom would be the leading abilities, and do check out VDA20 Tome of Secret's section on witchcraft for some details on making drugs and poisons and reproductive health.<br /> <br /> EDIT: as an addition: Cappadocians are particularly notorious for working closely with small mortal communities like monasteries and small towns, and for producing more ghouls than other clans. So it would not be an unusual set up for a Cappadocian to have a whole small village as his retinue, with several ghouls and therefore his identity as a vampire being barely - if at all - concealed.<br /> Paired with a Lamia it would be a fun duo: she brings disease to those she feeds from, while he keeps them healthy with outstanding healthcare and ghouling. I just need to check whether the illness brought by the Lamia's bite can be cured with Medicine rolls.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 05-26-2024, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T12:06:20-07:00","id":1536314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536295-dark-ages-can-you-be-a-vampire-in-sunlight?p=1536296#post1536296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just need to check whether the illness brought by the Lamia's bite can be cured with Medicine rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not mentioned whether it is treatable, IIRC. In older editions it is said to be 'much like' the Black Plague, which would mean no cure but the treatment of symptoms would enhance the chances of survival, if not by much. In VDA20 it deals one Lethal damage per night for two weeks, so strictly by RAW it should be survivable if that damage can be out-healed.<br /> <br /> Cainites living at least semi-openly in secluded communities during the Dark Ages isn't unheard of. An alternative to the philanthropic approach is having the character be local nobility who is powerful enough that even though the peasantry knows, they turn a blind eye out of fear. Those are mostly your Tzimisce voivodes.<br /> <br /> Both variants always carry the risk that eventually someone from inside the community will leak it to the church, no matter how thankful or afraid they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T04:30:43-07:00","id":1536336,"title":"","content":"Yes, the concept can work even if I could see two &quot;issues&quot; with it.<br /> <br /> One is that the Cainite in question would be pretty stationary to reap the rewards of his place in that village and that a whole coterie may be more Cainites than that village can support.<br /> <br /> The second is of course that the village would need to be pretty insular/isolated/xenophobic/whatever since if all the people in the village knows, its just a matter of time before someone slips a hint to an outsider that could lead to trouble, if they have much contact with outsiders to slip such hints from the start.<br /> <br /> Now playing a single Cainite in a village, which can't really hope for outside help in cause of problems, and dealing with issues that comes up, could be fun and offer its own scenarios but to me this sounds like a solo play character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T06:05:38-07:00","id":1536348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536295-dark-ages-can-you-be-a-vampire-in-sunlight?p=1536336#post1536336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the concept can work even if I could see two &quot;issues&quot; with it.<br /> <br /> One is that the Cainite in question would be pretty stationary to reap the rewards of his place in that village and that a whole coterie may be more Cainites than that village can support.<br /> <br /> The second is of course that the village would need to be pretty insular/isolated/xenophobic/whatever since if all the people in the village knows, its just a matter of time before someone slips a hint to an outsider that could lead to trouble, if they have much contact with outsiders to slip such hints from the start.<br /> <br /> Now playing a single Cainite in a village, which can't really hope for outside help in cause of problems, and dealing with issues that comes up, could be fun and offer its own scenarios but to me this sounds like a solo play character.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are good points. An option to make it more viable would be to have him linked to a nomad caravan rather than a village: he can benefit from his backgrounds even while travelling with a coterie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T07:50:00-07:00","id":1536358,"title":"","content":"I think the most viable way is a hybrid sort of character.<br /> <br /> Imagine a village which is a little bit remote but not totally disconnected from the trade lanes. The entire population knows the stories of the forest witch who lives near the community but apart from it. If you are brave enough to enter her section of woods or climb to her mountain cave etc. then you can speak with her. She might have great wisdom or insight, she could give you potion that heals you or makes you stronger, she might teach you forging techniques from a long-fallen empire, she might come to the village to slay the raiders which are pillaging it.<br /> <br /> The village elders know the truth of the matter that the &quot;forest witch&quot; is in fact a guardian vampire who was once a member of the village and has stuck around. Hence why they always suggest you bring a live goat or something similar as &quot;payment&quot; just to listen to your problems. The witch in the woods thing can work even better if the vampire has access to Animalism which allows it to keep track of what has been going on in the area, and make the villagers think that every animal in the area works for the vampire.<br /> <br /> Depending on if the vampires Animalism or Protean is high enough, there could be plenty of stories of an animal familiar or a shape shifted witch doing things in the village like outing a liar, leading lost children home, chasing off predators like bears or wolves.<br /> <br /> Being part of the community as a supernatural is possible, it just requires a bit of public relations management.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T08:16:26-07:00","id":1536362,"title":"","content":"Eh I would also say that the vampire could maybe a vampire on the path of Golconda. Because Golconda is intentionally left ambigious except the fact that Garou leave Vampires that reached Golconda alone because they are Holy instead of Corrupted. So if the said vampire has reached the enlightment of Golconda then yeah I think it is believeable that you could say for your game, that Golconda allows Vampires to go out at day unharmed by the sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T08:57:03-07:00","id":1536365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536295-dark-ages-can-you-be-a-vampire-in-sunlight?p=1536362#post1536362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh I would also say that the vampire could maybe a vampire on the path of Golconda. Because Golconda is intentionally left ambigious except the fact that Garou leave Vampires that reached Golconda alone because they are Holy instead of Corrupted. So if the said vampire has reached the enlightment of Golconda then yeah I think it is believeable that you could say for your game, that Golconda allows Vampires to go out at day unharmed by the sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Golconda also removes the Generation stat cap, which means that unless the enlightenment was recent, the power level will be approaching &quot;anime protagonist&quot; grade in short order, remember even the antediluvians are stat capped at 10 dots. Thus a 13th generation vampire who achieves Golconda with enough XP will be stronger than a 2nd Generation vampire and immune to the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T10:15:11-07:00","id":1536368,"title":"","content":"There is a much more likely and plausible play option than Golconda: the vampire character becomes a Background NPC, and the player character is their ghoul or revenant.<br /> Your interactions with kine become a lot easier, and the role stays basically the same. Perhaps you are a sorcerer or witch who agreed to serve in exchange for knowledge in the arcane arts. While you are handling the townsfolk, your master can stay low and focus on their studies, but is still there if some crisis calls for it. You just have to keep the Herd happy.<br /> <br /> Of course, that may defeat the point of playing an overt vampire, but it might be still interesting to play from a third-person POV, so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T02:00:19-07:00","id":1536412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536295-dark-ages-can-you-be-a-vampire-in-sunlight?p=1536368#post1536368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a much more likely and plausible play option than Golconda: the vampire character becomes a Background NPC, and the player character is their ghoul or revenant.<br /> Your interactions with kine become a lot easier, and the role stays basically the same. Perhaps you are a sorcerer or witch who agreed to serve in exchange for knowledge in the arcane arts. While you are handling the townsfolk, your master can stay low and focus on their studies, but is still there if some crisis calls for it. You just have to keep the Herd happy.<br /> <br /> Of course, that may defeat the point of playing an overt vampire, but it might be still interesting to play from a third-person POV, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay the question is, did op wanted to ask for a character for him to play or if the character itself could be part of the game. Because if it is for him self to play then Golconda is not feaseable option because Golconda is more of the end of a journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T15:16:52-07:00","id":1536538,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys and girls!<br /> <br /> You're giving me so much material to work on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T04:40:00-07:00","id":1536615,"title":"","content":"An good trick is to drop false memories with dominate of you being out during the day to reduce suspicion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T20:16:00-07:00","id":1536829,"title":"","content":"Not for very long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}